{"id": 17, "ts": 1780438727.9217832, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fB is the only one with documented operational reliability (\u201cvery conscientious\u201d) and proven stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d). However, Emily\u2019s note that B\u2019s professional communication can be pretentious and that we have no evidence of his crew\u2011cooperation raises a serious concern for the collaborative cockpit environment we need for long\u2011distance flights.\nGiven that reliability and stress handling are essential but must be paired with strong crew cooperation and respectful communication, I am less convinced that B should be our top choice. I will keep my vote open pending further input on the other candidates\u2019 reliability and cooperation, but at this point I am leaning toward Candidate\u202fC, who is explicitly described as 100\u202f% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, despite some communication style issues."}
